{
  "$comment": [
    "SHARED CROSS-LANGUAGE CONTRACT FIXTURE — one file, two suites.",
    "",
    "serverContract mirrors the constants of the authoritative validator",
    "(src/main/java/.../character/Char3DConfigValidator.java). The Java test",
    "ClientContractFixturesTest asserts every entry EQUALS the real constant, so this",
    "file can never drift from the server. The karma spec contract/server-contract.spec.ts",
    "then validates everything the shipped Angular client produces against these",
    "patterns, which is how a client that emits a value the server would 400 on gets",
    "caught in CI instead of in the user's face.",
    "",
    "acceptedDefinitions are VERBATIM payloads the shipped clients POST to",
    "/bff/character-forge/characters. ClientContractFixturesTest feeds each one to the",
    "real validator and requires it to be ACCEPTED; server-contract.spec.ts requires the",
    "client to still produce them. Both halves are needed: the Java half alone cannot see",
    "the client change, the TS half alone cannot see the server change.",
    "",
    "vnMapCases pin the DESIGN §2 mapping on both sides: VnMapService.map(vnCharacter)",
    "must equal canonical (Java), mapVnToChar3d(vnCharacter) must equal canonical (TS),",
    "and canonical must be a validator fixed point.",
    "",
    "vnPackCredits are the pack-level credit blocks of the four vendored VN manifests",
    "(src/main/resources/vn/packs/<packId>/pack.json), in Char3DConfigValidator.PACK_IDS",
    "order. ClientContractFixturesTest asserts they equal VnPackManifests.credits(), and",
    "server-contract.spec.ts asserts the Angular remote's vendored VN_PACK_CREDITS equals",
    "them — so the SRD 5.1 attribution the in-app credits view renders is the same string",
    "the manifests carry, VERBATIM, and a re-copied pack cannot silently change it."
  ],
